#: src/ch02-14-security-considerations.md:77
msgid ""
"Reentrancy vulnerabilities arise when a smart contract calls an external "
"contract before updating its state. This allows the external contract to "
"recursively call the original function, potentially leading to unintended "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

